{"name":"Morbid Princess","hex":"#9e0e64","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morbid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or afflicted by disease. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Taking an interest in, or fixating on, unhealthy or unwholesome subjects such as death, decay, disease."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morbid"},{"term":"princess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female member of a royal family other than a queen, especially a daughter or granddaughter of a monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A woman or girl who excels in a given field or class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess"}],"entries":[{"title":"Princess","blocks":[{"text":"Princess is a title used by a female member of a regnant monarch's family or by a female ruler of a principality. The male equivalent is a prince. Most often, the term has been used for the consort of a prince, or for the daughter of a monarch. A crown princess can be the heir apparent to the throne or the spouse of the heir apparent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/330px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/500px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/500px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Princess Sigrid Vasa of Sweden (1566–1633)[1][2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Prin